#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:1
msgid "Uploading model overlays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:3
msgid "Uploading model overlays requires the `Uploader` role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:5
msgid ""
"To upload model overlays, go to the [data "
"hub](https://vectoratlas.icipe.org/dataHub) page and click on `Upload "
"Model`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:7
msgid "![Data Hub page](datahub.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:7
msgid "Data Hub page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:9
msgid ""
"The model upload page requires a display name, maximum value for the data"
" and the model file itself. The display name is the name used on the map "
"in overlays section of the map tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:11
msgid ""
"The maximum value is needed because the overlay is transformed into a "
"tiled version for use in the map - this involves re-scaling the data to "
"match the grey scale colour map used by the system. It also means that "
"two overlays can be compared fairly, suppose two overlays represent a "
"percentage but the first has values between 0 and 10 but the second is "
"between 0 and 90. If the system scaled off the maximum value in the data "
"then it wouldn't be a fair comparison, by telling the system both have a "
"maximum value of 100 then the two layers can be compared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:13
msgid ""
"The model file must currently be a geotiff so that we can support "
"transformation into an mbtiles format. In the future there is planned "
"support for shape files as well as external tile servers (via wms)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:15
msgid "![Model upload page](model-upload.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:15
msgid "Model upload page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributing-data-to-the-atlas/uploading-model-outputs.md:17
msgid ""
"Once you click `Upload model` then the system will notify when the file "
"has been uploaded and that it's started to run the transformation, it "
"will then notify again if the transformation is successful or fails."
msgstr ""

